# Fixed 2026-09-29, defect 131's class, given to defect 133's lane. Symptom:
# `record Point )` over its fields was named `empty_record`, "a `record`
# needs at least one field, indented one level below it", while the fields
# stood one level down, and `variant Token )` over its cases was named
# `empty_variant` the same way: a message that names missing something that
# is there. Cause: the head's refusal asked only whether an indent followed
# the head, and junk on the head's own line stood in front of the one that
# did. The head's junk is now the one report, `expected_end_of_line` as a
# statement's line gets it, with where the members go, and the members are
# read as they stand, their own mistakes too. A head with junk and nothing
# below it is empty all the same, and says so.

record Point )  #~ expected_end_of_line
    x: i64
    y i64  #~ expected_field_type

record Lone )  #~ empty_record

variant Token )  #~ expected_end_of_line
    word
    number
        n f64  #~ expected_field_type

variant Nothing )  #~ empty_variant

function main()
    print(1)
